LLM yap:
The two CS35L63 amps are SPI sidecar amps hanging off the CS42L43 (they enumerate as spi-cs35l56-left/-right, driven by the cs35l56 driver, part 0x3563) — not SoundWire devices. The kernel only creates the cs42l43-cs35l56 bridge DAI that routes audio into these amps when the SOC_SDW_SIDECAR_AMPS quirk is set. That quirk is applied per-machine by the DMI table in sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c, keyed on Dell DMI_PRODUCT_SKU. This machine's SKU 0E53 was missing from the table, so the quirk stayed off → bridge DAI never created → external amps silent → only the CS42L43 internal amp plays

Signed-off-by: Eric Naim <dnaim@cachyos.org>
